<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Norodom of Cambodia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1834">1834</a>–<a href="/years/1904">1904</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as King Norodom, Norodom I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Norodom was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cambodia">Cambodia</a> from 1860 to 1904. Under pressure from Siam and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>, he accepted a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1863, and a convention imposed in 1884 handed most real power to French officials. His reign established the arrangement in which the Cambodian monarchy survived under French rule, and later kings, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norodom-sihanouk">Norodom Sihanouk</a>, descended from him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/norodom-of-cambodia.jpg" alt="Norodom of Cambodia" width="320" height="438" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Norodom,_the_King_of_Cambodia_Wellcome_V0037202.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
